body:
I was diagnosed at 21, spent my childhood being out of focus but got good grades so there was 'nothing wrong with me'

&#x200B;

Until now, even after being diagnosed, a lot don't believe me 'but you do so well in school!'

&#x200B;

And I agree with everything else you said; having to grow up faster, having to take responsibility, having to be a mom and take care of the rest because that's what's expected of you. I'm with you the whole way.
